## 1. OCB-HANKEL-03B — practical anytime composite-rank test

The Andreief determinant e-process is valid but power-poor.  Search for one matrix-valued or self-normalized e-process whose null is still a declared composite `rank<=3` class and whose evidence does not collapse to `det(H)`.  Stop if every safe construction is asymptotically determinant-limited.

A separate admissible route is an exact fixed-horizon composite e-value

`E_n = P_alt(data) / sup_{Q in H0} Q(data)`

for a **finite declared latent-class/HMM null**, followed by alpha-spending over a frozen checkpoint grid.  Do not call a local optimizer the supremum without a certificate.

